      "target": {
        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "QA-lab runtime-parity JSON bound",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\n`loadRuntimeParityMockToolCalls` in `extensions/qa-lab/src/runtime-parity.ts` parsed the mock debug endpoint body with unbounded `response.json()`. An oversized response could consume arbitrary memory.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nThe JSON body is now read with `readProviderJsonResponse` from `openclaw/plugin-sdk/provider-http`, which applies a 16 MiB byte cap and cancels the stream on overflow. This aligns the QA-lab runtime-parity path with other provider JSON readers.\n\n## User Impact\n\nRuntime parity comparisons are resilient to unexpectedly large mock debug responses; the runtime no longer buffers an unbounded JSON payload.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- Regression test added in `extensions/qa-lab/src/runtime-parity.test.ts` mocks an oversized JSON response and asserts `loadRuntimeParityMockToolCalls` returns null instead of buffering the body.\n- Real behavior proof script in `scripts/proof/qa-lab-runtime-parity-json-bound.mts` starts a local HTTP server returning a 20 MiB JSON-like body and verifies the bounded path discards it safely.\n\n### Local verification commands\n\n```bash\npnpm test extensions/qa-lab/src/runtime-parity.test.ts\nOPENCLAW_OXLINT_SKIP_PREPARE=1 node scripts/run-oxlint.mjs \\\n  extensions/qa-lab/src/runtime-parity.ts \\\n  extensions/qa-lab/src/runtime-parity.test.ts \\\n  scripts/proof/qa-lab-runtime-parity-json-bound.mts\nnode --import tsx scripts/proof/qa-lab-runtime-parity-json-bound.mts\n```\n\n### Proof script output\n\n```\n=== Proof: qa-lab runtime-parity JSON bound ===\n\nLocal server returning 20971520 bytes at http://127.0.0.1:38451\n\nPASS: oversized mock debug response was discarded (returned null).\n```\n\n\n---\n\nSupersedes #101130, which was auto-closed by the `r: too-many-prs` policy and could not be reopened via API.\n",
        "branch": "fix/qa-lab-runtime-parity-json-bound",
